  </article>
  </section><section style="margin:38px 0 0;">
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 20px;padding-bottom:9px;border-bottom:2px solid #111;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:25px;line-height:1.2;">Best of Asia</h2>
    <article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Closing soon</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://www.mori.art.museum/en/exhibitions/ronmueck/" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">Ron Mueck</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">Mori Art Museum · Tokyo, Japan</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#8b3d2e;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;">2026-04-29 – 2026-09-23</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">Mueck’s hyperreal figures manipulate scale until ordinary bodies become psychologically uncanny. This is a rare show that is immediately accessible without sacrificing depth.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://www.mori.art.museum/en/exhibitions/ronmueck/" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Official exhibition page →</a></p>
  </article><article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Opening soon</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://youmustchangeyourlife.kr/" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">16th Gwangju Biennale: You Must Change Your Life</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">Gwangju Biennale Exhibition Hall · Gwangju, South Korea</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#8b3d2e;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;">2026-09-05 – 2026-11-15</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">Ho Tzu Nyen is deliberately favoring concentration over the usual biennial sprawl. This is the strongest Asia art-trip candidate for autumn 2026 and worth planning before hotels tighten.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://youmustchangeyourlife.kr/" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Official exhibition page →</a></p>
  </article><article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Closing soon</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://www.nationalgallery.sg/PassionisVolcanic" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">Passion is Volcanic: Desire in Southeast Asian Art</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">National Gallery Singapore · Singapore</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#8b3d2e;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;">2026-04-24 – 2026-09-20</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">Rarely seen works examine desire, ritual, intimacy and politics across Southeast Asia. It combines serious regional scholarship with subject matter that feels alive rather than embalmed.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://www.nationalgallery.sg/PassionisVolcanic" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Official exhibition page →</a></p>
  </article><article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Worth noting</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">&quot;The Poetics of Survival&quot;: OPEN Architecture Designs Lina Bo Bardi&#039;s First Exhibition in China</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">Mainland China · archdaily.com</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#77716a;font-size:12px;">Reported 2026-08-17 · confirm dates in source</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">A specific institutional exhibition lead with enough scale or novelty to merit attention; the linked report contains the verified details and timing.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Read the source →</a></p>
  </article><article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">New exhibition</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">Ayala Museum exhibit features WWII diary of Japanese POW</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">Manila, Philippines · Inquirer.net</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#77716a;font-size:12px;">Reported 2026-07-12 · confirm dates in source</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">A specific institutional exhibition lead with enough scale or novelty to merit attention; the linked report contains the verified details and timing.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Read the source →</a></p>
  </article><article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Open now</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://www.leeumhoam.org/leeum/exhibition/93" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">Inside Other Spaces: Environments by Women Artists 1956–1976</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">Leeum Museum of Art · Seoul, South Korea</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#8b3d2e;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;">2026-05-05 – 2026-11-29</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">Walk-in, multisensory environments replace the usual art-at-a-distance experience. It is especially compelling for anyone interested in installations and the overlooked history of women building immersive spaces.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://www.leeumhoam.org/leeum/exhibition/93" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Official exhibition page →</a></p>
  </article><article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Plan ahead</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://www.nationalgallery.sg/sg/en/exhibitions/Pop-after-Pop-Art-around-Us.html" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">Pop after Pop: Art around Us</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">National Gallery Singapore · Singapore</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#8b3d2e;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;">2026-12-11 – 2027-04-04</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">More than 200 works will place American Pop beside Southeast Asian responses and legacies. It is worth flagging now for year-end travel, but not yet a reason to book a flight by itself.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://www.nationalgallery.sg/sg/en/exhibitions/Pop-after-Pop-Art-around-Us.html" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Official exhibition page →</a></p>
  </article>
  </section><section style="margin:38px 0 0;">
    <h2 style="margin:0 0 20px;padding-bottom:9px;border-bottom:2px solid #111;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:25px;line-height:1.2;">Worth Traveling For</h2>
    <article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Open now</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://www.labiennale.org/en/art/2026/61st-exhibition" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">Biennale Arte 2026: In Minor Keys</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">La Biennale di Venezia · Venice, Italy</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#8b3d2e;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;">2026-05-09 – 2026-11-22</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">Koyo Kouoh’s final curatorial project emphasizes multisensory work, collective practice and artists beyond the usual Western centers. It remains the world’s most consequential art trip of the year.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://www.labiennale.org/en/art/2026/61st-exhibition" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Official exhibition page →</a></p>
  </article><article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Open now</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://www.serpentinegalleries.org/whats-on/serpentine-pavilion-2026-by-isabel-abascal-and-alessandro-arienzo-lanza-atelier/" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">Serpentine Pavilion 2026 by LANZA atelier</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">Serpentine South · London, United Kingdom</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#8b3d2e;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;">2026-06-06 – 2026-10-25</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">LANZA atelier turns a curving brick wall into a permeable garden room. It is a strong art-and-architecture stop, especially paired with the Soto installation nearby.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://www.serpentinegalleries.org/whats-on/serpentine-pavilion-2026-by-isabel-abascal-and-alessandro-arienzo-lanza-atelier/" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Official exhibition page →</a></p>
  </article><article style="margin:0 0 28px;padding:0 0 24px;border-bottom:1px solid #e7e3dc;">
    <span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 8px;padding:3px 8px;border:1px solid #bbb;border-radius:999px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;">Open now</span>
    <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;"><a href="https://www.serpentinegalleries.org/about/press/serpentine-kickstarts-summer-programme-with-new-public-sculpture-by-jesus-rafael-soto/" style="color:#111;text-decoration:none;">Jesús Rafael Soto: Pénétrable BBL Jaune</a></h3>
    <div style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#625d56;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;">Serpentine South · London, United Kingdom</div>
    <div style="margin:0 0 9px;color:#8b3d2e;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;">2026-06-16 – 2026-10-25</div>
    <p style="margin:0;color:#292724;font-size:15px;line-height:1.62;">Visitors can physically enter Soto’s field of suspended yellow strands, making movement and touch part of the work. It is the first outdoor UK presentation of the artist’s work.</p>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;"><a href="https://www.serpentinegalleries.org/about/press/serpentine-kickstarts-summer-programme-with-new-public-sculpture-by-jesus-rafael-soto/" style="color:#6d3d2d;">Official exhibition page →</a></p>
  </article>
  </section>
    <p style="margin:34px 0 0;padding:18px 20px;background:#f5f1e9;color:#3b3834;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;"><strong>Editorial note:</strong> Closing-soon shows rise to the top automatically; newly reported items are included only when the headline and source establish the location rather than merely implying it.</p>
    <p style="margin:34px 0 0;color:#8a857d;font-size:11px;line-height:1.55;">Curated weekly for Kevin · Curated official listings form the quality floor; live discovery adds current, source-grounded leads without inventing titles, locations, dates or links. · Confirm final hours and ticketing before traveling.</p>
